<form class="totalform help-on-hover help-box" data-method="POST" data-route="/admin/settings/backups"><div class="form-field toggle-field " data-type="toggle" style="--grid-area: enable;"><label for="field-UID">Keep Object History</label><div class="form-group"><div class="switch"><input id="field-UID" name="enable" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="help-UID" checked/><label for="field-UID" aria-hidden="true">Keep Object History</label></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Master switch. When off, saves and deletes write no snapshots. Existing snapshots are left in place and still restore. Sync's pre-overwrite snapshots are unaffected by this setting.</p></div><div class="form-field number-field " data-type="number" style="--grid-area: keep;"><label for="field-UID">Snapshots per Object</label><div class="form-group"><input type="number" id="field-UID" name="keep" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="10" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="10" min="1" max="100" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">The newest snapshots each object keeps; older ones are pruned on the next save. Identical consecutive saves do not stack a duplicate. Raise this on a busy editorial site; it only costs the size of the record's JSON per snapshot.</p></div><div class="form-field number-field " data-type="number" style="--grid-area: maxAgeDays;"><label for="field-UID">Maximum Age (days)</label><div class="form-group"><input type="number" id="field-UID" name="maxAgeDays" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="30" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="30" min="0" max="3650" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Snapshots older than this are pruned regardless of the count above — one busy afternoon of edits would otherwise evict last week's version, the one you actually wanted. Set to <code>0</code> to keep snapshots until the count limit alone removes them.</p></div><div class="form-inline-fields"><button type="submit" class="button btn cms-save cms-button">Save Settings</button></div></form>